WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.118
This practice combines raw values with derived
metrics Sales and costs are the inputs

00:00:07.026 --> 00:00:12.934
Profit is the dollar amount remaining after costs
Margin compares profit with sales

00:00:13.184 --> 00:00:18.810
so it is naturally expressed as a percentage Run the
example and then

00:00:18.836 --> 00:00:24.668
increase the costs Watch what happens to both profit
and margin One

00:00:24.694 --> 00:00:29.523
value is an amount while the other is a ratio so
they communicate different aspects

00:00:29.536 --> 00:00:35.587
of performance Also notice that the margin
calculation divides by sales

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:40.997
In real analytical code we would eventually need to
consider what happens if sales are

00:00:41.023 --> 00:00:46.484
zero That kind of validation will become easier
after we learn conditions in the next

00:00:46.497 --> 00:00:47.063
module
